    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, from the request hitting the filter chain through to the response.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Security / authorization** *(validation)* \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on the handler. Requires the `OWNER_ADMIN` role. Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; otherwise security is disabled. (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:140`)\n\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** *(validation)* \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` + interface-level `@Validated` run JSR-380 constraints before any controller code. On failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 HTTP 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Constraints (`OwnerFieldsDto`):\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n   - `postcode`, `sharesHousehold`: no bean constraint; `registrationDate`, `birthDate`: ISO date format only\n\n## Inside the controller body (in this exact order)\n\n3. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`; ignores `id`, `pets`, `customerCode`. (`:144`)\n\n4. **Address normalization** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `addressNormalizer.normalize()` (trim/collapse/upcase/expand ST\u2192STREET). (`:145`)\n\n5. **Address blank check** *(validation)* \u2014 if normalized address is blank \u2192 **400**. (`:146`) Then `owner.setAddress(normalized)` *(side-effect, :149)*.\n\n6. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** *(validation + side-effect)* \u2014 `telephoneNormalizer.toE164()`; if it can't produce a valid E.164 number \u2192 **400**. (`:150\u2013152`)\n\n7. **Email normalization + validation** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 `emailNormalizer.normalize()`, then if email present and (not valid format **or** disposable domain) \u2192 **400**. (`:155\u2013157`)\n\n8. **Postcode validation** *(validation)* \u2014 if postcode present and `postcodeValidator.isValid(postcode, city)` fails \u2192 **400**. (`:159\u2013160`)\n\n9. **Registration date not-in-future check** *(validation)* \u2014 if a supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 **400**. (`:162\u2013164`)\n\n10. **Registration date roll-forward** *(side-effect)* \u2014 defaults null to today, then `BusinessDay.rollForward(...)`, and `owner.setRegistrationDate(...)`. (`:166\u2013168`)\n\n11. **Daily cap check** *(validation)* \u2014 `clinicService.countOwnersByRegistrationDate(date) >= 100` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**. (TX1, readOnly) (`:169\u2013170`)\n\n12. **Apply normalized telephone & email** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `setTelephone(e164)`, `setEmail(email)`. (`:172\u2013173`)\n\n13. **Per-city cap check** *(validation)* \u2014 `clinicService.countOwnersByCity(city) >= 50` \u2192 **409 Conflict**. (TX2, readOnly) (`:174\u2013175`)\n\n14. **Household-occupied check** *(validation)* \u2014 if `sharesHousehold` is not true and `clinicService.isHouseholdOccupied(owner)` \u2192 **409 Conflict**. (TX3, readOnly) (`:180\u2013182`)\n\n15. **Set declared household member flag** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `owner.setDeclaredHouseholdMember(sharesHousehold)`. (`:184`)\n\n## Persistence (`clinicService.saveOwner`, TX4 read-write) \u2014 `:185`\n\nOnly when `owner.isNew()`, in order:\n16. **Generate customer code** if null \u2014 SHA-256-based `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. *(side-effect)*\n17. **Set namesake count** \u2014 case-insensitive count of matching first+last name. *(side-effect)*\n18. **Set bulk-signup warning** \u2014 true if same-day registrations > 80. *(side-effect)*\n19. **Set household id** \u2014 SHA-256 of `lastName|postcode` (null if no postcode). *(side-effect)*\n20. **Set household size**. *(side-effect)*\n21. **Possible-duplicate detection** \u2014 `findPossibleDuplicate(...)`; sets `possibleDuplicate` and `possibleDuplicateOf`. *(side-effect)*\n22. **Persist** \u2014 `ownerRepository.save()` \u2192 `em.persist(owner)`, which triggers:\n    - **`@PrePersist normalizeRegistrationDate()`** \u2014 defaults null date to today and re-applies `BusinessDay.rollForward` (a second normalization at the JPA layer). *(side-effect)*\n    - **Entity-level constraints** enforced on flush: `Owner` (`@NotEmpty` address/city; telephone `@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`), `Person` (`@NotEmpty` firstName/lastName). A violation surfaces as a DB/constraint exception handled by the advice. *(validation)*\n    - **ID assignment** via `@GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)`.\n    - TX4 commits when `saveOwner` returns.\n\n## After the write\n\n23. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerAuditLogger.logCreated(owner)` writes id/customerCode/registrationDate to the `\"AUDIT\"` logger; runs **after** TX4 commits, outside any transaction. (`:186`)\n\n24. **Build response** *(side-effect)* \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (adds computed `displayName`), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 Created**. (`:187\u2013190`)\n\n## Ordering notes worth flagging\n\n- The controller method is **not** `@Transactional`; the three count/household checks (steps 11, 13, 14) each run in their own read-only transaction *before* the separate write transaction (step 22), so the caps are **not** isolated against concurrent inserts.\n- `registrationDate` is rolled forward twice \u2014 once in the controller (step 10) and again in `@PrePersist` (step 22).\n- `CallMonitoringAspect` exists but is **not wired** (no `@Component`/`@EnableAspectJAutoProxy`), so it does not intercept this path.\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
